=====

## Slide 8 — Security severity overview (Default Slide, Title + Upsubtitle)
- Title: "Security: 4 findings"
- Upsubtitle: "No CRITICAL — but two HIGH around OS command execution"
- Body: BlockGrid 1×4 of HERO_METRIC_ON_TOP:
  - "0" CRITICAL
  - "2" HIGH
  - "1" MEDIUM
  - "1" LOW

=====

## Slide 9 — Security findings list (Default Slide, Title only)
- Title: "Security — all 4 findings"
- Body: BlockGrid 2×2 of blocks (no icon needed; severity-tagged short titles)
  - "HIGH — Missing AUTHORITY-CHECK before SFTP GET"
    - No explicit auth check before `SXPG_COMMAND_EXECUTE` (SFTP pull path).
  - "HIGH — Missing AUTHORITY-CHECK before SFTP PUT"
    - Same gap on the push path; relies only on FM `no_permission` exception.
  - "MEDIUM — Shell-injection risk in parameters"
    - `gv_param` built by unescaped CONCATENATE from `zfi_constants-fval`.
  - "LOW — Sensitive details leaked via WRITE"
    - `OPEN DATASET` error messages reveal filesystem paths to the user.

=====

