## Slide 18 — Maintainability findings 1/2 (Default Slide, Title only)
- Title: "Maintainability — findings 1–8"
- Body: BlockGrid 4×2 of compact "LOW —" titled blocks, 1-line each
  - "LOW — Obsolete CONCATENATE for path build" — use string templates.
  - "LOW — Magic value for log-color param" — raw `'6'/'4'/'3'` literals passed around.
  - "LOW — Magic literals in FORMAT COLOR CASE" — same color codes hard-coded again.
  - "LOW — `WITH HEADER LINE` (lt_return #1)" — obsolete table-with-header declaration.
  - "LOW — `WITH HEADER LINE` (lt_return #2)" — second instance of the same pattern.
  - "LOW — Commented-out code left in place" — stray `*lv_doc` declaration above active one.
  - "LOW — `SPLIT` for filename parsing" — older style; consider FIND REGEX.
  - "LOW — Dead variable `lv_userid`" — declared, cleared, never sourced.

=====

## Slide 19 — Maintainability findings 2/2 (Default Slide, Title only)
- Title: "Maintainability — findings 9–16"
- Body: BlockGrid 4×2 of compact "LOW —" titled blocks
  - "LOW — Mixed inline vs top DATA in same FORM" — inconsistent declaration style.
  - "LOW — Hard-coded business text 'INVALID PATIENT ID'" — should use message class.
  - "LOW — CONCATENATE for message build" — replace with string template.
  - "LOW — Magic constant `'AU1'` (document type)" — extract to named constant.
  - "LOW — Commented-out `ENDIF` left behind" — control-flow noise.
  - "LOW — Hard-coded allowed-characters string" — opaque validation set.
  - "LOW — CONCATENATE for path with `'\\'` separator" — magic separator + obsolete style.
  - "LOW — Untyped FORM parameters in `f_fill_log`" — implicit ANY typing.

