## Slide 25 — Retro: lessons (Default Slide, Title only)
- Title: "What we learned for the next run"
- Body: BlockGrid 2×2 of blocks with icons
  - "Worked well" (icon: Checkmarks / Checkmark_Circle_1)
    - Parallel category checks safe with read-only tools.
    - Per-category isolation — no rule leakage.
    - Strict source citation eliminated speculation.
  - "Went off" (icon: Checkmarks / X_Mark_Circle_1)
    - Bash backtick expansion mangled rule text in prompts.
    - Severity-summary regex missed maintainability block.
  - "Fix next time" (icon: Processes / Repair if available else Gear_Process_2)
    - Build prompts in Python end-to-end, no bash variables.
    - Parse severity from per-finding headings only.
  - "Don't change" (icon: Goals / Thumbs_Up)
    - One worked example per pipeline is enough.
    - Keep parallelism only for read-only tool sets.

